---

Iconoclastic is an adjective describing someone or something that attacks, challenges, or ignores cherished beliefs, traditions, or institutions. It implies a rebellious, nonconformist approach—often in art, politics, or religion—that breaks with established conventions. The term originates from the literal destruction of religious icons